    "summary": "Live runs are a count per run id (orchestrator/live-runs.ts; isRunLive is exported). runAnalyze raises the count before its first read of a run record and lowers it when it returns or throws. Its stages moved into runStages, which runAnalyze guards from that first read: an uncaught error is written to the run record as failed at the stage reached with 'internal-error' and returned, 'done' fires once, the stage starts as 'classify', and the handler's own write is guarded. The tests run whole runs with no model (a stated source and size on a sandboxed store); an uncaught error is raised by a signal whose 'aborted' cannot be read, and an unwritable record by a directory where the record's file goes. Eleven mutations: ten caught (the three named ones among them), one a deliberate equivalent control; one surviving mutation (the handler ignoring the record last written) led to a stronger assertion and is now caught. Nothing reads isRunLive yet: the abandoned rule is task t14.",
